Drop `maxHeartbeats 0` from the two UniformizerClauseOfAdmitted proofs.

`set_option maxHeartbeats 0` turns off Lean's time limit for a declaration, so
a proof that loops or blows up would never stop. These two proofs do not need
it. Measured by compiling each file with different limits after building its
dependencies (about 580 modules, all of which compiled):

  dual_lemma_of_admitted       fails at 850,000, passes at 906,250
  local_lemmas_of_literature   fails at 687,500, passes at   750,000

The project limit in lakefile.toml is 4,000,000, so each proof now runs under
it with more than four times headroom. Both modules build with `lake build`.
Nothing else in the files changes.

